### Exercise 3 - Error 2 (part 3 of 3): 403 Forbidden
# POST /api/tickets (the legacy, non-v1 endpoint) requires ADMIN specifically.
# A USER-role token is authenticated but not authorized for this one.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "title": "Should be forbidden",
  "description": "Testing 403 with a USER-role token",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "LOW",
  "createdBy": "testuser@example.com"
}


### Exercise 3 - Error 3: 400 Bad Request
# Invalid priority value fails @Pattern validation on UpdateTicketRequest.
# Get a real ticket id from GET /api/v1/tickets first and paste it below.
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tickets/paste-ticket-id-here
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Test",
  "description": "Test",
  "category": "Test",
  "priority": "URGENT",
  "status": "OPEN"
}


### Exercise 3 - Error 4: 404 Not Found
# A well-formed but non-existent MongoDB ObjectId.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tickets/000000000000000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Exercise 3 - Error 5: 409 Conflict
# Registering the same email twice triggers DuplicateResourceException.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "TestUser@12345"
}
